l-linux raniel-linux    4096 Oct 30 12:26 tmp\n-rw-r--r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux    1059 Oct 30 12:30 validation-complete.log\n1657891 executor-finish.stdout\n  11089 executor-p1.stdout\n1904130 executor.stdout\n   2153 gpt-final-audit.stdout\n   4903 sarah-final-audit.stdout\n3580166 total\n**NO-GO for the local candidate. P0: 0. P1: 3.**\n\n1. **Partial ingress reopening is falsely recorded as complete.**  \n   Location: `first_transition_host_driver.py::_inspect_host`; `first_transition_host_contract.py::resume_legacy`.  \n   Reproduction: resume all four legacy services; opening `evolution-backend` succeeds, then opening `external` times out before taking effect. Replay `resume_legacy`. Because `ingress_blocked` means **both blocked**, the partially open state reports `False`. Replay skips `open_ingress`, accepts `not ingress_blocked`, and records `observed-host-resumed` while external ingress remains blocked. Recovery reports success without restoring service.\n\n2. **The “DDL-free” proof accepts schema changes omitted from its fingerprint.**  \n   Location: `first_transition_database.py::Q_CATALOG`, `require_ddl_free`, `LedgerProof.prove`.  \n   Reproduction: establish the expected baseline, then execute `ALTER TABLE public.notification_outbox ALTER COLUMN claimed_until SET DEFAULT now()` outside this journal, without updating the migration ledger. The fingerprint excludes defaults; relation/attribute identity, ledger, invalid indexes and index builds remain unchanged. `LedgerProof` consequently accepts the altered schema and permits legacy resume. Changes to policies, function bodies and constraint definitions have the same coverage gap.\n\n3. **Incomplete configured lease coverage can authorize DDL with active leases.**  \n   Location: `first_transition_orchestrator.py::parse_config`; `first_transition_database.py::ReadOnlyDatabase.__init__`, `_observe`.  \n   Reproduction: supply `lease_columns=[[\"notification_outbox\",\"claimed_until\"]]`; leave that table unclaimed while `broadcast_entregas.lease_ate` contains a future lease. Configuration accepts this nonempty subset. With other containment checks satisfied, both quiet observations report `active_leases=0`, allowing the DDL marker and migrations despite the outstanding broadcast lease. Missing mandatory lease coverage therefore fails open.\n\nThese are control-flow findings from the supplied bytes; no execution or environment verification was performed.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05249313-2279-499a-9431-55b58a17e539","uuid":"2bb31172-8358-4d08-9c72-49c609919e86","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:45:11.955Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"total 3968\ndrwxrwxr-x 3 raniel-linux raniel-linux    4096 Oct 30 12:45 .\ndrwxrwxr-x 3 raniel-linux raniel-linux    4096 Oct 30 12:03 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux      19 Oct 30 12:37 acceptance-ruff.log\n-rw-r--r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux     703 Oct 30 12:37 acceptance.log\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux    1476 Oct 30 12:38 audit-source-hashes.json\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux     869 Oct 30 12:35 executor-blockB-pytest.log\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux      19 Oct 30 12:35 executor-blockB-ruff.log\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux       0 Oct 30 12:29 executor-finish.stderr\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux 1657891 Oct 30 12:36 executor-finish.stdout\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux    5325 Oct 30 12:03 executor-instructions.txt\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux       0 Oct 30 12:45 executor-p1.stderr\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux   11089 Oct 30 12:45 executor-p1.stdout\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux     112 Oct 30 12:03 executor-state.json\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux       0 Oct 30 12:03 executor.stderr\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux 1904130 Oct 30 12:27 executor.stdout\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel-linux  358328 Oct 30 12:40 gpt-final-audit.stderr\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 raniel-linux raniel